            "text": "An efficient implementation in Python that balances memory usage and execution speed using BLAS matrix multiplication in double precision:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef main():\n    # Load input array\n    vectors = np.load(\"vectors.npy\")\n    X = vectors.astype(np.float64)\n    del vectors\n\n    # Squared L2 norms of each vector\n    sq_norms = np.sum(X**2, axis=1)\n\n    # Compute Gram matrix G = X @ X.T using BLAS dgemm\n    G = X @ X.T\n    del X\n\n    # In-place calculation of squared Euclidean distances:\n    # ||u - v||^2 = ||u||^2 + ||v||^2 - 2 <u, v>\n    G *= -2.0\n    G += sq_norms[:, None]\n    G += sq_norms[None, :]\n\n    # Ensure diagonal is exactly 0 and numerical precision errors don't cause negatives\n    np.fill_diagonal(G, 0.0)\n    np.maximum(G, 0.0, out=G)\n\n    # Element-wise square root to get Euclidean distances\n    np.sqrt(G, out=G)\n\n    total = float(np.sum(G))\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
